,{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.6962,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Klint Kubiak"},{"season":2022,"team":"NO","distance":0.7511,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Pete Carmichael"},{"season":2020,"team":"CLE","distance":0.7859,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.7979,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2020,"team":"DAL","distance":0.6167,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"MIN","distance":0.6222,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.656,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2024,"team":"SEA","distance":0.7104,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2021,"team":"IND","distance":0.7109,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Raiders went 8-8 in 2020 and were outscored 478 to 434. The offense carried the team, ranking 13th in EPA per play while the defense finished 29th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits were the 2nd highest 22 personnel usage and the 2nd highest Cover 6 rate in the league.","offense":"The Raiders offense was a little above average by EPA per play. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 2nd highest 22 personnel usage and the 3rd highest 13 personnel usage in the league. Derek Carr ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Darren Waller, who drew 28% of the targets.","defense":"The Raiders had one of the worst defenses in the league, ranking 27th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, pressure rate, only ranked 14th, and it was 30th in takeaways per game. Maxx Crosby was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Nicholas Morrow, who had 3 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. In terms of scheme, they had the 2nd highest Cover 6 rate in the league.","special":"The Raiders were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 94% of field goals, which was well above average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their tight ends were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Derek Carr played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,103 yards. Darren Waller was the clear top target with 28% of the looks and 1,196 receiving yards. Josh Jacobs handled most of the work in the backfield with 67% of the carries. On defense, Maxx Crosby led the team with 7 sacks and Jeff Heath picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2019 Broncos and the 2024 Saints under Klint Kubiak. Their defense looked most like the 2020 Cowboys and the 2019 Vikings.","trends":"The offense went from 10th in EPA per play in 2019 to 13th in 2020, a modest decline. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2019 to 29th in 2020, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was singleback usage, which went from 30% to 23%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2020. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}